==Icelandic==
[[File:Iris - right eye of a girl.jpg|thumb|Eitt auga.]]
===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|auga}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*augô}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*h₃ekʷ-|t=eye; to see}}. Cognates include {{cog|la|oculus}}, {{cog|sa|अक्षि|tr=ákṣi}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐌿𐌲𐍉}}, {{cog|ang|ēaġe}}, {{cog|en|eye}}, {{cog|sco|ee}}, {{cog|sv|öga}}, {{cog|da|øje}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈøyːɣa]|lang=is}}
* {{audio|is-auga.ogg|Audio|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|øyːɣa|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|auga|augu}}

# {{lb|is|anatomy}} [[eye]]
#* [[w:en:Hávamál|Hávamál]] ([[s:en:Poetic Edda/Hávamál|English source]], [[s:is:Hávamál|Icelandic sourve]])
#*: ''Inn vari gestur''
#*: ''er til verðar kemur''
#*: ''[[þegja þunnu hljóði|þunnu hljóði þegir]],''
#*: ''eyrum hlýðir,''
#*: ''en '''augum''' skoðar.''
#*: ''Svo nýsist fróðra hver fyrir.''
#*:: The knowing guest
#*:: who goes to the feast,
#*:: In silent attention sits;
#*:: With his ears he hears,
#*:: with his '''eyes''' he watches,
#*:: Thus wary are wise men all.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-n-w||au|g|n=n}}

